  "result": "Ownership handover is implemented. The full suite passes (74 files, 632 tests, up from 617 with the 14 new handover tests and one new errors case), and `tsc --noEmit` is clean.\n\nChoices I made where the spec left room:\n- **Offering and withdrawing** require the owner role (a new owner-only `org:transfer_ownership` action) and recorded ownership. A recorded owner who has been demoted to admin can't offer.\n- **Acceptance** runs its writes in order (promote the acceptor, repoint the owner, demote the previous owner, resolve the offer), but not in a DB transaction, since the codebase has none.\n- **Removing the recorded owner** leaves `organizations.owner_id` pointing at the removed member. The spec didn't cover this, and it means that member keeps receiving new-member alerts.\n- **The offer notification** links to `/settings/members`. There is no accept or decline UI yet.",
